    {
      "commentary": {
        "commtxt": "B0$ Whatever may happen from here, one thing looks almost certain in this edition of the CPL - the Guyana Amazon Warriors are heading for the playoffs. They are second on the points table, have already begun their home leg with a comprehensive win over the Jamaica Kingsmen, and have four more home games to come over the next week. Most importantly, they remain the only unbeaten side in the competition. Standing in their way today are the St Kitts and Nevis Patriots, who arrive on the back of two successive wins. A victory for Guyana would take them to the top of the table, while a win for the visitors would see them climb to third.",
